    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1143">

                <pb facs="1512" n="1502" sameAs="frus:frus1945v03/pg1502"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 EW/1–446</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in France</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1946-01-04T19:00:00-05:00">January 4, 1946—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>36. For Angell. Reurtel 175 Dec. 24.<anchor n="22" xml:id="d1143-f1"/> While this
                    Govt has no objection to the proposal that the final disposition of German
                    assets in the disputed areas shall remain in suspense until the territorial
                    questions have been settled, nevertheless it perceives no advantage in endorsing
                    the resolution proposed by the Yugoslav delegate. Such endorsement might be
                    interpreted as supporting Yugoslav claims to the Julian March before final
                    decision on this point is reached at the Council of Foreign Ministers.
                    Furthermore the recent instructions sent to the American Ambassador at
                        Belgrade<anchor n="23" xml:id="d1143-f2"/> with regard to the constitution
                    of the new Yugos Govt would preclude endorsement of the resolution for “reasons
                    of political prestige”.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Byrnes</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1143-f1" n="22" xml:id="d1143-f1-content">
                <p>See telegram 7329, December 24, 2 p.m., from Paris, <ref target="#pg1487">p.
                        1487</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1143-f2" n="23" xml:id="d1143-f2-content">
                <p>The instructions were sent to Ambassador Patterson on December 22; see Department
                    of State <hi rendition="#italic">Bulletin</hi>, December 23, 1945, p. 1020.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
